{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":202840,"ns":0,"title":"Adjugate matrix","extract":"In linear algebra, the adjugate or classical adjoint adj(A) of a square matrix A is the transpose of its cofactor matrix. It is occasionally known as adjunct matrix, or \"adjoint\", though that normally refers to a different concept, the adjoint operator which for a real matrix is the transpose.","description":"For a square matrix, the transpose of the cofactor matrix","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}